1
00:00:01,000 --> 00:00:05,354
A content part adds data, an editor, and a display to the content

2
00:00:05,354 --> 00:00:06,704
items of a type.

3
00:00:06,704 --> 00:00:09,464
This video covers the pieces of a part:

4
00:00:09,464 --> 00:00:13,941
its class, its display driver, its templates, and its registration.

5
00:00:13,941 --> 00:00:17,130
The example is the Title part of Orchard Core.

6
00:00:21,730 --> 00:00:25,537
A content part groups the data for one purpose, such as a title,

7
00:00:25,537 --> 00:00:27,984
with the screens that edit and show it.

8
00:00:27,984 --> 00:00:32,770
You attach parts to a content type, and every content item of that type gets them.

9
00:00:33,520 --> 00:00:35,110
A part has four pieces.

10
00:00:35,110 --> 00:00:39,166
A class holds its data, a display driver builds the shapes that edit

11
00:00:39,166 --> 00:00:43,826
and show it, templates render those shapes, and a registration and a definition

12
00:00:43,826 --> 00:00:45,470
make the part available.

13
00:00:46,220 --> 00:00:48,278
The driver never writes HTML.

14
00:00:48,278 --> 00:00:52,745
It creates shapes, which are objects that hold the data to display and

15
00:00:52,745 --> 00:00:55,450
the information about how to display it.

16
00:00:55,450 --> 00:00:59,800
Orchard Core then finds the template for each shape, and renders it.

17
00:01:04,000 --> 00:01:08,707
The class derives from ContentPart, and its public properties hold the data.

18
00:01:08,707 --> 00:01:11,003
TitlePart has one property, Title.

19
00:01:11,003 --> 00:01:16,170
Orchard Core saves the properties with the content item, under the name of the part.

20
00:01:16,920 --> 00:01:20,957
The view model is a plain class that carries what the templates need.

21
00:01:20,957 --> 00:01:25,478
TitlePartViewModel has the Title, and also the content item, the part, and the

22
00:01:25,478 --> 00:01:29,300
settings, marked BindNever so that model binding never sets them.

23
00:01:30,050 --> 00:01:35,606
A migration calls AlterPartDefinitionAsync to define the part by the name of its class.

24
00:01:35,606 --> 00:01:41,222
Attachable lists it among the parts you can add to a content type, with its description.

25
00:01:41,222 --> 00:01:43,970
A separate video covers data migrations.

26
00:01:48,170 --> 00:01:54,482
The display driver derives from ContentPartDisplayDriver, with the part as its type argument.

27
00:01:54,482 --> 00:01:59,200
The constructor receives a string localizer, for the error messages.

28
00:01:59,200 --> 00:02:01,751
The work happens in three methods:

29
00:02:01,751 --> 00:02:04,110
Display, Edit, and UpdateAsync.

30
00:02:04,860 --> 00:02:08,681
Display returns a display result that builds one shape.

31
00:02:08,681 --> 00:02:12,816
Initialize creates a strongly typed shape from a view model.

32
00:02:12,816 --> 00:02:17,890
The lambda fills in its properties, and the part is passed in as its state.

33
00:02:18,640 --> 00:02:24,024
GetDisplayShapeType names the shape TitlePart, and adds the display mode of the part,

34
00:02:24,024 --> 00:02:25,207
if it has one.

35
00:02:25,207 --> 00:02:27,692
Location places the shape in a zone:

36
00:02:27,692 --> 00:02:32,130
the Title part uses Header, for the Detail and Summary display types.

37
00:02:32,880 --> 00:02:37,018
A driver can return null to display nothing, as the Title part does

38
00:02:37,018 --> 00:02:40,985
when there is no title, or when its Render Title setting is off.

39
00:02:40,985 --> 00:02:46,200
A shape with no location isn't displayed either, unless a placement rule gives it one.

40
00:02:46,950 --> 00:02:53,062
Edit builds the shape of the editor from the content item, and GetEditorShapeType names it TitlePart_Edit.

41
00:02:53,062 --> 00:02:56,937
It sets no location, because the editor shape of a part goes into

42
00:02:56,937 --> 00:02:59,120
the shape of that part by default.

43
00:02:59,870 --> 00:03:02,481
UpdateAsync runs when the form is posted.

44
00:03:02,481 --> 00:03:06,036
TryUpdateModelAsync copies the posted value into the part.

45
00:03:06,036 --> 00:03:09,868
The prefix, which is the name of the part, keeps its form field

46
00:03:09,868 --> 00:03:12,590
names apart from the fields of other parts.

47
00:03:13,340 --> 00:03:15,058
The driver then validates.

48
00:03:15,058 --> 00:03:18,977
An error added to the model state keeps the content item from being

49
00:03:18,977 --> 00:03:21,876
saved, and the editor is built again to show it.

50
00:03:21,876 --> 00:03:26,440
The base class stores the part back in the content item, so the driver doesn't.

51
00:03:30,640 --> 00:03:34,179
A Razor file in the Views folder of the module is the template

52
00:03:34,179 --> 00:03:35,324
of a shape type.

53
00:03:35,324 --> 00:03:38,760
Dots in a file name stand for underscores in the shape type.

54
00:03:38,760 --> 00:03:43,600
The Title part has templates for the display, the Summary display type, and the editor.

55
00:03:44,350 --> 00:03:47,649
The display template is Razor over the view model:

56
00:03:47,649 --> 00:03:48,945
here, a heading.

57
00:03:48,945 --> 00:03:53,481
The editor template binds an input to the Title property, and shows the

58
00:03:53,481 --> 00:03:56,250
validation message that UpdateAsync adds.

59
00:03:57,000 --> 00:04:01,333
The Summary template, for the Summary display type, renders the title as a

60
00:04:01,333 --> 00:04:04,800
link to the content item, with the display-for tag helper.

61
00:04:09,000 --> 00:04:12,790
In the Startup class, AddContentPart registers the part.

62
00:04:12,790 --> 00:04:18,659
UseDisplayDriver connects the driver to every display mode and editor, and AddHandler adds

63
00:04:18,659 --> 00:04:21,777
a handler for the events of the content item.

64
00:04:21,777 --> 00:04:24,650
AddDataMigration registers the migration.

65
00:04:28,950 --> 00:04:30,459
Let's use the part.

66
00:04:30,459 --> 00:04:36,255
Under Design, Content Definition, Content Types, choose Create new type, enter Workshop as

67
00:04:36,255 --> 00:04:38,790
the Display Name, and choose Create.

68
00:04:39,273 --> 00:04:41,829
The next page lists the parts you can add.

69
00:04:41,829 --> 00:04:45,131
Title is there, with the description from its migration.

70
00:04:45,131 --> 00:04:48,273
Add & Configure adds the part and opens its settings.

71
00:04:48,846 --> 00:04:53,910
Under Behavior option, choose Title is editable and required, and choose Save.

72
00:04:53,910 --> 00:04:59,216
This setting belongs to the Title part, and its driver reads it when it validates.

73
00:05:03,516 --> 00:05:07,210
Under Content, Content Items, New Workshop opens the editor.

74
00:05:07,210 --> 00:05:12,806
The Title field comes from the editor template, rendered from the shape that the driver built.

75
00:05:13,294 --> 00:05:15,828
Choose Publish with the field empty.

76
00:05:15,828 --> 00:05:21,802
UpdateAsync adds an error, the item isn't saved, and the editor shows again with the message:

77
00:05:21,802 --> 00:05:23,974
A value is required for Title.

78
00:05:24,503 --> 00:05:27,694
Enter a title, Pruning Apple Trees, and choose Publish.

79
00:05:27,694 --> 00:05:31,513
The part is saved with the content item, and the page confirms that

80
00:05:31,513 --> 00:05:33,553
your Workshop has been published.

81
00:05:34,015 --> 00:05:35,795
Choose View to open the page.

82
00:05:35,795 --> 00:05:39,713
The Display method placed the shape in the Header zone, and the display

83
00:05:39,713 --> 00:05:42,105
template rendered the title as a heading.

84
00:05:42,583 --> 00:05:44,632
Back in the list, choose Edit.

85
00:05:44,632 --> 00:05:49,412
The editor shows the saved title, because UpdateAsync copied it to the display

86
00:05:49,412 --> 00:05:52,883
text of the content item, and Edit reads it from there.

87
00:05:57,083 --> 00:06:00,669
A part can have settings for each content type, as the Title part

88
00:06:00,669 --> 00:06:02,688
does with its own settings driver.

89
00:06:02,688 --> 00:06:06,274
A handler reacts to events of the content item, as the handler of

90
00:06:06,274 --> 00:06:09,303
the Title part does to generate titles from a pattern.

91
00:06:10,053 --> 00:06:12,660
The locations in a driver are defaults.

92
00:06:12,660 --> 00:06:16,368
A placement file can move or hide a shape, and a theme can

93
00:06:16,368 --> 00:06:19,033
replace a template for one content type.

94
00:06:19,033 --> 00:06:22,103
Separate videos cover placement and alternates.

95
00:06:24,103 --> 00:06:28,246
A part is a class, a display driver, its templates, and a registration

96
00:06:28,246 --> 00:06:32,225
with a definition, and together they put your own part in the admin

97
00:06:32,225 --> 00:06:34,786
and on your site, as the Title part does.

98
00:06:34,786 --> 00:06:36,203
Thanks for watching.

